'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  ch06-current-drive-blink.spin2
''   Purpose....  The same blink, but choosing the drive strength the pin
''                uses to get there
''   Manual.....  P2 I/O & Smart Pins User Guide
''   Version....  v1.0.9 (2026-08-18)
''   Appears in.  Chapter 6: Digital Output -- 6.5 Worked Examples
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Jun 2026
''   Updated....  Jun 2026
''
''   This file is an EXAMPLE from the manual above. Everything below
''   this header is byte-identical to the listing printed there --
''   what you read in the manual is what builds here.
''
'' ===========================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq = 200_000_000
  LED_PIN = 56
  BLINK_MS = 500

PUB main()
  ' Current-source for consistent brightness
  WRPIN(LED_PIN, P_HIGH_1MA | P_LOW_FAST)
  
  repeat
    PINHIGH(LED_PIN)
    WAITMS(BLINK_MS)
    PINLOW(LED_PIN)
    WAITMS(BLINK_MS)

